e slow methodical  meaning you feel the weight of your  weapons  you have a stamina gauge and can't just  repeatedly attack without some sort of  negative repercussion  the world design is interconnected and  you'll find looping and branching paths  as well as shortcuts that bring you back  to earlier points in the game  while i've been showing footage of the  soulsborne games all of these elements  are right here in this little gem  so let me rewind and give you the exact  same speech  but with king's field footage  you start in a location with branching  paths there are definitely routes you  shouldn't take and are far too difficult  for you but the game won't hold your  hand and trust the player to discover  for themselves the correct path to go  meanwhile it's actually okay to travel  these paths if you can accept the  challenge  there is a story but it's not completely  spoon fed to you and you'll have to look  at item descriptions to get a fuller  picture of what's going on there are  locations with hidden traps that have  been set for you which you can also  utilize against your enemies  the game is notoriously challenging and  forces you to figure out the mechanics  yourself  there are a plentiful amount of hidden  walls and truss falls onto hidden ledges  with both secret items and weapons for  you to find in other words secrets that  are actually meaningful and exciting to  get your weapon attacks are slow  methodical meaning you feel the weight  of your weapons  you have a stamina gauge and can't just  repeatedly attack without some sort of  negative repercussion  the world design is interconnected and  you'll find looping and branching paths  as well as shortcuts that bring you back  to earlier points in the game now while  i can tell you this and show you this  it's better if hiratake miyazaki shows  you himself  this is just a random paper i decided to  use as a prop  kingsfield was the beginning of the  demon souls project i wouldn't go as far  as to 