e majority of  the time if you take one of these risks  you'll be rewarded with an interesting  item and i truly mean something you'll  probably want to use whether it be a  weapon a cool spell a key or some type  of special use item i tend to overuse  this example but in many of the zelda  games your reward for exploration is a  box of rupees and while that's fine a  lot of times you won't really need or  want it however in king's field i've  never found myself annoyed at the reward  i received for exploration and while  you're not always rewarded you usually  are and it makes it that much more  meaningful  on top of that some of the secrets are  [ __ ] cool in one instance i found a  painting that said locked but couldn't  find the key  so i attacked the painting which killed  the painting and ended up being the way  to unlock this particular secret in  another instance a merchant was blocking  my way to an expensive item  rather than buying it from him i pushed  him out of the way by constantly  stabbing him stole it and then found it  was no longer for sale the game actually  took into account this random mechanic  of being able to slowly push npcs by  attacking them you'll find standard  puzzles where you shoot fireballs and  light lamps or perhaps minecarts you'll  have to jump off of in the middle of  your ride to find another hidden secret  then there's the map design the  labyrinth of my personal favorite  kingsfield games kingsfield one in the  us and kingsfield for the ancient city  are genuinely interesting with plenty of  unique areas you'll find you'll also  often find yourself exploring deeper  into an area that feels genuinely  intimidating and oftentimes will take  you out of your comfort zone but in a  good challenging kind of way  on top of that they often wrap within  themselves with surprising shortcuts and  secrets you'll unlock that show just how  smartly interconnected the map design is  then there's the music unlike many of  the modern from soft games kingsfield  has consistent music playing throughout  the game which is atmospheric and spooky  these tracks add to the mood and creep  factor of games that honestly  graphically don't hold up that great  outside of ps2s the ancient city in fact  i often use these tracks in the  background of my soul's lore videos as  ambiance since they suit the mood of  those games just as well then there's  the moonlight greatsword many of you  will know this from demon souls or  perhaps dark souls or perhaps the  bloodborne dlc  but the moonlight greysword first  appeared in the japanese king's field  and has become somewhat of a mascot for  from software in fact it's even made an  appearance in armored core and i bring  this up because a lot of the dna of from  software goes all the way back  to king's field it was a niche game made  for a niche audience just like demon  souls but like the souls games it  tackles that niche with a degree of  excellence now look  maybe i have some rose tinted glasses on  and i'm overly nostalgic about the game  but  every time i go back to replay my  favorite kings field games i fall in  love all over again  and that's not true of every game and  the thing is i am so glad from software  has finally been discovered so to speak  because it's not just king's field  inspired by king's field from software  also made the shadow tower games which  share a similar design philosophy to  king's field only even more challenging  as your weapons now break on top of that  they created the armored core franchise  which has for the longest time been one  of the best mech series out there now  not every game by from software has been  a masterpiece and admittedly i haven't  played all of them eternal ring was okay  ninja blade i hear is anything but good  however  in my humble opinion from software  deserve to be on the map before dark  souls blew them up and i'm glad  i'm glad so many people finally  understand how incredible this company  is and how amazing the games they  develop are i'm glad they're able to  continue to make amazing games and so  excited that they still maintain an  uncompromising vision to their games  hitataki miyazaki has taken the spirit  of king's field and brought it into  demon souls and dark souls  although  i still want a new king's field  thanks so much for watching me ramble  about a game that means so much to me  graphically speaking i know it can be  rough for many but i truly think the  core design of these games are  impeccable and i just want more people  to know about it  anyways this is part of a series of from  software videos we're making in  preparation for eldon ring so make sure  to come back for more from us at  gamespot and from myself  [Music]  you

